{"abi":[],"bytecode":{"object":"0x","sourceMap":"","linkReferences":{}},"deployedBytecode":{"object":"0x","sourceMap":"","linkReferences":{}},"methodIdentifiers":{},"rawMetadata":"{\"compiler\":{\"name\":\"solar\",\"version\":\"0.8.38+commit.e7a91fc7.solar.0.3.0-dev\"},\"language\":\"Solidity\",\"output\":{\"abi\":[],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{},\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{},\"notice\":\"\\n * StdChains provides information about EVM compatible chains that can be used in scripts/tests.\\n * For each chain, the chain's name, chain ID, and a default RPC URL are provided. Chains are\\n * identified by their alias, which is the same as the alias in the `[rpc_endpoints]` section of\\n * the `foundry.toml` file. For best UX, ensure the alias in the `foundry.toml` file matches the\\n * alias used in this contract, which can be found as the first argument to the\\n * `_setChainWithDefaultRpcUrl` call in the `_initializeStdChains` function.\\n *\\n * There are two main ways to use this contract:\\n *   1. Set a chain with `setChain(string memory chainAlias, ChainData memory chain)` or\\n *      `setChain(string memory chainAlias, Chain memory chain)`\\n *   2. Get a chain with `getChain(string memory chainAlias)` or `getChain(uint256 chainId)`.\\n *\\n * The first time either of those are used, chains are initialized with the default set of RPC URLs.\\n * This is done in `_initializeStdChains`, which uses `_setChainWithDefaultRpcUrl`. Defaults are recorded in\\n * `_defaultRpcUrls`.\\n *\\n * The `setChain` function is straightforward, and it simply saves off the given chain data.\\n *\\n * The `getChain` methods use `_getChainWithUpdatedRpcUrl` to return a chain. For example, let's say\\n * we want to retrieve the RPC URL for `mainnet`:\\n *   - If you have specified data with `setChain`, it will return that.\\n *   - If you have configured a mainnet RPC URL in `foundry.toml`, it will return the URL, provided it\\n *     is valid (e.g. a URL is specified, or an environment variable is given and exists).\\n *   - If neither of the above conditions is met, the default data is returned.\\n *\\n * Summarizing the above, the prioritization hierarchy is `setChain` -> `foundry.toml` -> environment variable -> defaults.\\n \",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"lib/crane/lib/forge-std/src/StdChains.sol\":\"StdChains\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/test/mocks/\",\"battlechain-lib/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/src/\",\"battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/\",\"chainlink-ccip/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/vendor/optimism/interop-lib/v0/src/\",\"chainlink-evm/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-evm/\",\"chainlink-local/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/src/\",\"clones/=lib/crane/contracts/external/clones-with-immutable-args/\",\"contracts/external/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/=lib/crane/contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/\",\"contracts/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"crane/=lib/crane/\",\